+# Development Diary — October 2026
+
+## 2026-10-16: Preserve page fullscreen through SDL startup
+
+- SDL applies initial windowed flags while showing its game canvas. Its
+  Emscripten driver previously exited document fullscreen even when the page's
+  HTML element owned it, so fullscreen entered from the launcher was lost at boot.
+- Keep SDL fullscreen exit scoped to its own canvas. Apply the permanent,
+  hash-pinned SDL patch independently of optional input diagnostics.
+- Fullscreen entry and mouse capture use separate gestures; canvas capture follows
+  successful entry, and late capture grants after fullscreen exit are released.
+
+Validation: the actual pinned driver function fails the page-owned fullscreen
+fixture before patching and passes afterward, while canvas exit, windowed startup
+and SDL fullscreen entry still pass. Patch idempotence and source drift checks
+pass; all 17 fullscreen/pointer-lock tests pass. New WASM/browser verification
+follows in the wrapper integration.
+
+## 2026-10-16: Prepare clean source builds for cloud CI
+
+- Verify the FFmpeg and FreeType source archives against pinned SHA-256 values.
+  Allow the wrapper to bound FFmpeg compilation jobs alongside the engine jobs.
+- The independent wrapper reconstructs this engine from the pinned upstream and
+  maintained patch, verifies its source tree, bootstraps the pinned SDK/build
+  tools and open Liberation fonts, and exports without a private installation.
+  Diagnostics remain an explicit build/export opt-in.
+
+## 2026-10-16: Validate the repaired game in Chrome
+
+- Audio-fixed candidate a1d919cfc1b8 ran about 20 minutes on one page, including
+  more than 12 minutes on GC_TankGeneral. Same-map JS heap stayed 65.5–188.4 MiB
+  including startup (last 96.8 MiB), AL PCM stayed 14.391–14.974 MiB, and SDL
+  enqueue failures/queue invariant errors stayed zero while input worked.
+- The final e8385a5e5b0b binary differs only by the separately tested shutdown
+  order. Record the bounded session evidence without claiming all longer
+  sessions are proven. Final Chrome smoke passed startup, intro/Esc, menu clicks,
+  healthy SDL/audio snapshots and acknowledged manual reporting.
+
+## 2026-10-16: Release audio resources before context shutdown
+
+- Stop active audio and destroy the cache while the OpenAL context is current;
+  then close the device/context. Previously cache deletion ran after the context
+  was cleared, where SDK alDeleteBuffers cannot release retained PCM.
+- A separate fixture compiles the exact production destructor/closeDevice bodies
+  and current cache with real SDK OpenAL. Current ordering passes eight checks;
+  old methods with the same cache fail four cleanup/PCM/device checks.
+- This is a shutdown fix; active-game ownership and the real-game soak candidate
+  are otherwise unchanged. WebAudio plumbing remains controlled in the fixture.
+
+## 2026-10-16: Add temporary OpenAL allocation snapshots
+
+- Under the existing OFF-by-default gates, sample main-thread OpenAL counts,
+  actual WebAudio float32 bytes, unreferenced buffers and pending AL error at
+  30-second cadence. Never capture buffer objects/identities or clear AL errors.
+- This distinguishes PCM retention from WASM/allocator memory in the next
+  same-mission real-game comparison. No per-frame resource-table scan is added.
+
+## 2026-10-16: Account resident audio storage in the cache budget
+
+- Charge decoded PCM instead of replacing its size with compressed file bytes.
+  Emscripten OpenAL stores WebAudio float32 samples, so account that expansion
+  for 8/16-bit input. Reject entries which cannot fit the budget before adding
+  their charge, preventing overflow and unnecessary eviction.
+- Real SDK OpenAL regression verifies 8/16-bit decoded buffer sizes and actual
+  WebAudio float32 storage/cache charges, separately from ownership tests.
+
+## 2026-10-16: Repair OpenAL cache ownership and sample transitions
+
+- The real Chrome heap retained about 1.19 GB in 4,750 OpenAL audio buffers;
+  4,702 had zero source references. New cache entries incorrectly started with
+  zero leases, allowing active eviction to forget a buffer after OpenAL rejected
+  deletion, and first-close counters could unsigned-wrap.
+- Admit the first lease only after decode/budget success, guard unmatched closes,
+  and retain ownership/accounting when actual buffer deletion fails. Keep the
+  cache entry available during reentrant source cleanup.
+- Stop and detach old sample buffers before closing cache leases at all loop
+  and attack/sound/decay transitions; stopped sources still retain AL_BUFFER.
+- The actual production cache linked with SDK OpenAL reproduces failures on the
+  baseline and passes 17 ownership/transition/deletion checks after the fix.
+  Post-fix real-game memory trend remains to be validated.
+
+## 2026-10-16: Clarify diagnostic provenance and removal
+
+- Attribute browser-main pointer callbacks to SDL's existing Emscripten backend,
