+# Browser input freeze investigation — 16 October 2026
+
+## Failure boundary and mechanism
+
+The reported production session continued advancing simulation frames after SDL
+polled/input counters stopped. DOM input and SDL raw button state still changed.
+Existing reports did not measure SDL's internal queue, so its exact corrupted
+state in that session remains unproven.
+
+The browser build used `SDL_PTHREADS=OFF`, SDL's Emscripten default even with
+compiler `-pthread`. This selects `SDL_THREADS_DISABLED` and no-op mutexes.
+SDL's Emscripten backend installs pointer callbacks on the browser main thread
+(`Emscripten_set_pointer_event_callbacks`); these call its WASM pointer handler
+directly, while `PROXY_TO_PTHREAD` runs game polling on a worker. This path also
+exists without Pointer Lock. The custom cursor/Pointer Lock integration uses
+that existing SDL path; it did not introduce these direct callbacks. The shared queue therefore lacked synchronization. SDL's
+thread identity, TLS and error buffers also used the threadless backend.
+Keyboard callback proxying can differ; direct pointer callbacks alone establish
+the unsafe concurrency.
+
+A specific interleaving orphans the queue: while cutting sole event E, the
+consumer sets head=E.next=null. The producer appends N through old tail E and
+sets tail=N. The consumer then sees E is no longer tail and leaves tail=N.
+Later pushes append to the unreachable chain, while polling sees null head.
+Raw state can keep changing while event delivery remains stopped.
+
+## Actual-library reproduction
+
+The maintained C harness links the real SDL archive; an isolated threadless
+baseline never replaces the game archive:
+
+```sh
+GX_WEB_DIAGNOSTICS=1 bash scripts/build.sh
+python3 scripts/build-sdl-diagnostics-test.py
+python3 scripts/build-sdl-diagnostics-test.py --raw-pthread-stress
+# Expected failures: reproduce the old unsupported-thread configuration/race.
+python3 scripts/build-sdl-diagnostics-test.py --threadless-baseline
+python3 scripts/build-sdl-diagnostics-test.py --threadless-baseline --raw-pthread-stress
+```
+
+Correctly threaded SDL passes 18 primary checks: 4,096 concurrent ordered events,
+filter rejection, full 65,535-event queue failure, shutdown and disabled probes.
+The old library fails `SDL_CreateThread` because threads are unsupported.
+
+Raw-pthread stress simulates actual browser/worker concurrency without SDL
+thread creation. The old library reproduced the orphan on its first round:
+138/4,096 events consumed, internal count=3,958, head absent, tail present.
+A repeat consumed 170, count=3,926, with the same invariant failure. Corrected SDL
+delivered all 524,288 ordered events with zero inconsistencies. Stress scheduling
+is nondeterministic; a passing run alone does not exclude all possible races.
+
+The permanent fix explicitly enables the supported `SDL_PTHREADS` backend and
+rejects configuration if it cannot be built. This is strong mechanism evidence;
+long real-game sessions are still required to validate the production scenario.
+No queue reset, watchdog, synthesized input or simulation change is introduced.
+
+## Separate supported permanent fixes
+
+- Remove old font/glyph/caption/tooltip and nonerror INI trace producers before
+  Emscripten worker transport. Preserve real INI and font-add errors.
+- Delete owned WebGL textures/FBOs and vertex/index buffers at final COM release;
+  retain render-target parents through rebind/reset/destruction; bound shader
+  programs using 256-entry LRU eviction. Actual GPU fixtures fail on the starting
+  baseline and pass after the fixes (130 resource checks, 13 shader/draw checks).
+  Emscripten's GL IDs still grow monotonically: deleted slots no longer retain
+  GL objects, but table capacity can grow.
+- The earlier approximately 3 GB browser JS heap is not a measurement of WASM
+  memory or proof of its 4 GB limit. New probes distinguish both independently.
+
+## Temporary probes, gates and removal
+
+`GX_WEB_INPUT_DIAGNOSTICS` defaults OFF. The default build has no old/new C++
+counters, generated telemetry bridge or SDL probe symbols. Explicit ON defines
+only six input boundary sources and the SDL target. A maintained pinned SDL 3.4.2
+patch validates the pristine source hash, applies idempotently and rejects drift.
+
+Browser export/runtime additionally defaults OFF and requires `--diagnostics`.
+The compile manifest binds mode to the successful WASM hash and rejects an
+instrumented export of a compiled-off/stale engine. Server writes default OFF;
+an ignored generated config enables only the current debug deployment in the
+existing Pages project. Access identities/JWTs, private R2 and retention stay
+unchanged. Exported source includes independent engine-version provenance.
+
+Five-second bounded snapshots include poll/early-return counts, public pending
+count, filter/event-enabled state, atomic push/enqueue/filter/full/allocation
+failures, sentinels, and locked internal count/head/tail-presence invariants.
+Separate bounded game/main-runtime SDL error strings are copied without clearing
+errors. WASM pages reconstruct exact bytes even at 4 GiB. dlmalloc used/free/arena
+is sampled every 30 seconds to limit free-list walking. Numeric sample sequences
+and SDL/browser timestamps correlate streams; no typed keys or raw pointers are
+recorded. Probes do not filter, drain or reset input.
+
+The browser ring/chunks/retries are bounded and preferentially retain eight
+recent engine/browser samples during interaction storms. Disable restores hooks,
+removes listeners, cancels timers/RAF/observers, aborts requests and discards
+persisted retries. Current clients poll the server gate every 30 seconds. Older
+already-open versions cannot be rewritten remotely: server rejection blocks
+writes, and reload closes their old collector lifecycle.
+
+See the wrapper hosting guide for opt-in collection and exact shutdown/removal
+commands. Remove the complete temporary overlay, including the original
+collector/probes preserved in the pre-existing baseline; blindly reverting the
+OFF-gate commits would restore that old always-enabled collector. Keep gates
+OFF until all probes/hooks/routes are removed together. Retain permanent
+logging, WebGL, SDL synchronization and OpenAL lifetime/residency fixes, and rebuild SDL from fresh
+dependency sources after removing its maintained diagnostics patch.
+
+
+## Follow-up: actual OpenAL heap retention
+
+The first real-game candidate retained approximately 1.19 GB across 4,750
+OpenAL PCM buffers. Offline heap analysis found 4,702 zero-reference buffers
+holding more than 99.3% of those PCM bytes; active references held about 7.21 MiB.
+This identifies orphaned audio storage independently of the SDL queue race or
+WebGL table capacity. The source cache admitted new buffers with zero playback
+leases. Eviction could then skip source cleanup, fail actual OpenAL deletion,
+and erase the only cache handle. First-close counters could also unsigned-wrap.
+Stopped sources retained AL_BUFFER across loop/portion transitions after the
+cache lease had already been closed, allowing another failed-deletion path.
+
+Permanent audio changes initialize admitted leases, guard unmatched closes,
+retain entries/accounting when deletion is rejected, and detach sources before
+releasing loop/portion cache ownership. A separate change charges decoded PCM,
+including WebAudio float32 expansion, instead of compressed file bytes. The
+actual production cache linked against SDK OpenAL fails on baseline ownership
+and pre-accounting revisions and passes after the fixes. The fixture stubs only
+file/FFmpeg input and AudioContext plumbing, not OpenAL refcount/deletion rules.
+
+Temporary snapshots now include live AL buffers/sources, actual float32 PCM
+bytes, zero-reference buffer counts and the pending AL error without clearing
+it. They scan numeric resource metadata only once per 30 seconds. No speculative
+GL instrumentation or queue recovery was added.
+
+## Post-fix real-game comparison
+
+The audio-fixed Chrome candidate `a1d919cfc1b8` ran on the same local origin for
+approximately 20 minutes, including more than 12 minutes continuously on
+`GC_TankGeneral`. Stored same-map samples through 11:59:27 UTC showed JS heap
+65.5–188.4 MiB (including mission startup), last 96.8 MiB. Actual AL float32
+storage stayed 14.391–14.974 MiB, last 14.644 MiB. SDL enqueue failures and
+queue invariants remained zero, simulation advanced and manual input worked.
+This replaces the earlier same-map growth of roughly 130 MiB/minute and the
+1.19 GB orphaned PCM capture with a bounded observed interval; it does not prove
+that every longer session or other scenario is free of leaks or input stalls.
+
+The final binary `e8385a5e5b0b` adds only the separately tested shutdown-order
+fix to that soak candidate: it destroys cached audio before closing the context.
+Active-game code and telemetry are unchanged between those two builds. Final
+Chrome smoke passed: Play, intro, Esc to the main menu, single-player submenu
+clicks, healthy SDL/audio snapshots and an acknowledged manual diagnostic
+report. Default-OFF build checks, actual-library regressions and Pages Functions
+bundling also pass.
